     "text": "This was a people’s period. Elections of 1977 were held in the country and the Pakistan National Alliance, after its defeat, accused the government of irregularities and started a movement, which took the form of the Tehreek-e-Nizam-e-Mustafa (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, his family and companions). In the country, on 5 July 1977 General Muhammad Zia-ul-Haq imposed martial law and all important politicians were arrested. General Zia made significant amendments in the Constitution of 1973 and increased his powers enormously. In 1985, holding non-party elections, he appointed Muhammad Khan Junejo as Prime Minister. The important measures of General Zia’s period were these:",
