   "theory": "… awareness. Issuing driving licences, patrolling roads and putting duty at crossings, maintaining traffic and law and order on roads, preventing accidents and reaching the scene of accidents is the responsibility of the police. Planning to solve traffic problems in cities and getting traffic laws respected is the duty of the police. To determine the legal status of vehicles it has its own scientific investigation centres. On every important road and crossing young police personnel stand ready for public service. If the police did not perform this responsibility, how many accidents would take place daily and how much illegal and criminal traffic would go on.\n\nAt the district level there are two branches of the police:\n\n1. Investigation Branch\n\n2. Operational Branch\n\n1. Investigation Branch:\n\nThis branch of the police prepares cases. In every district it has its own head. This branch prepares the cases registered in police stations for presentation in court. Maintaining the record of correspondence between the court and the police and of cases is the responsibility of this branch. This branch is in contact with the other branches of the police in the preparation of cases. In important and …",
