   "content": "<p>Children</p><p>Every human being is a child who is in the early age and who depends on parents. He is not capable of stepping into practical life and self-reliance. Different countries have fixed an age limit for children which is not uniform all over the world. According to the CRC (Convention on Right of Children), a child means every human being whose age is less than eighteen years.</p><p>Need of a Convention on the Rights of Children</p><p>All over the world excesses are committed against children. Their basic rights keep being trampled, and most children face inhuman behaviour. Throughout the world the custom of forced labour of boys and girls was becoming common. This oppression was found to a dangerous extent in developing and backward countries.</p><p>Orphaned, helpless, poor and disabled children have faced inhuman attitudes, whose control is in every respect the responsibility of the civilised world.</p><p>Children too are human beings, and they are innocent, who are in dire need of the love of parents and the affection of society. Children need health, education and upbringing, and care. Parental supervision and care are needed. Special facilities and recreational places are urgently needed for them from parents and the government. Therefore the need for such a convention was felt so that parents and the government could be compelled to perform their duties.</p><p>At the world level the convention on the rights of children was approved and enforced, but perhaps the purpose has still not been achieved. Violations of children’s rights are continuing. New ways and manners of violating children’s rights are being adopted. Therefore …</p>",
