   "content": "<p>13. According to Article 38, children shall be kept away from wars to the extent possible for the state, and children shall not be recruited into the army. War-affected children shall be given special protection and attention.</p><p>14. According to Article 40 of the convention, all legal requirements and precautions shall be kept in view for punishing children, and it shall be kept in mind that during this time a sense of dignity is created in children and they become respecters of human rights and freedoms. So that children become capable of being active members of society.</p><p>Provision of Rights of Children in CRC</p><p>The rights of provision given in the world convention on children’s rights are as follows:</p><p>1. In the preamble of the convention states have been urged that there is a need to provide special help and attention to children.</p><p>2. Under Article 4 states have been bound to ensure the provision of the rights given to children in this convention, and to take legislative, administrative and other suitable measures for this purpose. States, remaining within their resources and making use of world cooperation, shall ensure the provision of children’s economic, social and cultural rights.</p><p>3. According to Article 6.2, party states shall ensure the survival and development of children to the extent possible.</p><p>4. According to Article 7 of the convention, states shall ensure the provision of these rights of children: that after birth their registration be done; from birth the right to keep a name; the right to be given nationality; and the right to care and attention from parents.</p><p>5. According to Article 8, states shall ensure respect for children’s rights so that children can protect their identity, which includes their nationality, name and relation with the family etc., and unlawful interference in these rights is prevented. If any part of identity is taken away from any child, states shall provide him help and protection in restoring his identity …</p>",
