   "content": "<p>… is. Respect for human rights should be created in children; recognition of their own self and culture, recognition of their own language and national values; children should be prepared for responsible practical life so that they can understand peace, tolerance, gender equality and friendship etc.</p><p>13. According to Article 39 of the convention, states are bound to ensure the provision of suitable measures and facilities for such children who have been victims of neglect, exploitation, misuse, torture, inhuman behaviour or punishments and war etc.</p><p>Rights of Participation to Children in CRC</p><p>In the Convention on the Rights of the Child the following measures are mentioned for ensuring the participation of children:</p><p>1. According to Article 9, children cannot be separated from their parents without their will, so that they have the right of participation in family life.</p><p>2. According to Article 12, regarding the interests of children their opinion will have to be given importance. In this the age and understanding of the child will have to be kept in view.</p><p>3. According to Article 13, children have the right to freedom of expression, including searching for, obtaining and spreading ideas and information, but not at the cost of anyone’s dishonour, national security, peace and morals.</p><p>4. According to Article 14, states will respect children’s freedom of thought, conscience and religion.</p><p>5. According to Article 15 of the convention, states will have to recognise the freedom of children to organise and to hold peaceful assemblies …</p>",
