     "text": "In the CRC, emphasis has been placed on respecting the self-esteem of children. According to Article 16 of the convention, the protection of the honour and reputation of children shall be ensured. According to Article 37, states are bound to provide protection to children from inhuman, torturous and cruel punishments and behaviour. According to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, his family and companions), the self-esteem of children should be taken care of. Before Islam the Arabs considered children their personal property (estate). The Quran strictly negated this. In the world convention on children this too has been negated. According to Article 19, for states it is necessary to take suitable legislative, administrative and social and educational measures to save the child from physical and mental violence, injury or their misuse, neglect, bad behaviour and exploitation etc. In the Quran, in nineteen verses, harsh and cruel behaviour with orphan boys and girls has been prohibited. It is the right of children that they be saved from physical and moral harm. In Islam children have been given the right of inheritance.",
