   "content": "<p>Negative Impacts of Globalization</p><p>Because of globalisation very negative effects are also being produced on the culture of Pakistan, like other developing countries. World institutions and their members are a means of cultural penetration in Pakistan. Their magazines, booklets, radio and television broadcasts are polluting the culture of developing countries including Pakistan. We are facing a cultural onslaught. The harms of mobile phones and the internet are hidden from no one. Religious, moral and cultural values are being uprooted. Change is clearly taking place in dress, customs, habits, language and literature, ways and lifestyle, rituals and traditions and morals etc.</p><p>Pakistan is a developing country, and in an ordinary world economic market Pakistani goods are weak in comparison with developed countries. In this way local industry will suffer a blow. In this respect local industries will be ruined, because even within the country they cannot compete with world multinational corporations. International institutions give their employees big salaries and facilities which, in comparison with Pakistani institutions, are many times more and attractive. In this way balance does not remain either, and Pakistan’s experts take interest in these world institutions while they leave the national institutions. All these things are pointing to a journey towards a bad economic situation.</p><p>Essentials of Self-Reliant Economy</p><p>Self-reliance means that an individual or country depends on itself instead of depending on others. That is, it is a form of self-respect. Several basic conditions or requisites are needed for a self-reliant economic system. If these are ensured, the economic system does not depend on any particular support. The very first condition for self-reliance is that loans and aid from other nations are not expected at all. If a nation becomes addicted to this intoxication, stillness is created in its activities. Such nations go nowhere and remain waiting for loans and charity. This way of working also ends the possibilities of progress and going ahead. Therefore it is necessary that external loans and aid be discouraged to a large extent. The great powers, through several financial institutions …</p>",
