   "content": "<p>… are available, because of which local products are facing a severe crisis. If domestic products and other goods are given preference, this is in favour of self-reliance.</p><p>For self-reliance it is necessary that positive and durable reforms be made in all the institutions of the country. Changes should be made in the administrative, political, social and economic structures of the country according to new needs, desires and demands. That is, every system and every machinery will have to be prepared for new conditions, difficulties and activities. It is not possible that other aspects move towards self-reliance and the structure of the country does not change; otherwise all efforts go to waste. A simple life is very important for self-reliance. The greater the simplicity, the less the dependence on others. Simple food, simple housing, simple dress and the use of natural things is the best cure for the disease of dependence. An extravagant life is troublesome not only for oneself but also for others. Therefore simplicity is useful besides the good and blessing of religion and world, for national interests too. If non-development expenditures are reduced, national capital can be saved. The unlimited facilities of senior government employees should be reduced. The government should control its non-development expenditures. The expenditures of ministers and members of the assembly should be reduced, and the lavish spending of rulers should be controlled. Non-development expenditure in offices should be reduced as much as possible, and there is an urgent need to pay attention to development activities. In this way a self-reliant system can be achieved.</p><p>International Financial Institutions (Functions and Objectives)</p><p>1. World Bank</p><p>The World Bank, or the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development, was formed on 27 December 1945 when 29 countries of the world signed a mutual agreement in the Bretton Woods conference.</p>",
