   "content": "<p>5. Protection of the environment.</p><p>This bank divides its work into several sectors, i.e. agriculture and natural resources, energy, industry and minerals, finance, means of transport and communication, and social structure etc. In its Article number 1 the aim of the bank in Asia has been stated to be to make economic development fast.</p><p>Functions</p><p>To fulfil the above-mentioned objectives the bank is performing the following functions:</p><p>1. Promoting investment for development purposes in member countries.</p><p>2. Providing financial cooperation to the development process by one’s own will, and giving priority to those regional and national projects which help in balanced and overall development. Giving special attention to small and less developed member countries.</p><p>3. Cooperating with them, at the request of member countries, in their development policies and plans, so that they can make correct use of their resources and promote mutual trade.</p><p>4. Providing technical help in the preparation of special development plans, financial aid and the implementation of these plans.</p><p>5. Cooperation with the United Nations and all its agencies in similar objectives.</p><p>Political Impacts of International Financial and Economic Institutions</p><p>World financial and economic institutions have political effects on both the aid-givers and the aid-takers. Politics and economy cannot be separated from each other, and both have deep and lasting effects on each other. Behind world aid, cooperation and loans etc. there are political objectives at work. Experts are of the view that world aid is an important weapon of the foreign policy of the aid-giving country. World institutions too are made by individuals and economically strong states …</p>",
