     "text": "Industry and industrial products are a very important source of the country’s income. By preparing high-quality goods at low cost, exports can be increased, because of which the country’s role in world trade can increase. Capital can come into the country, which can become a cause of discouraging world loans. To promote the trend towards industrialisation the government should announce incentives and concessions. Investment should be encouraged and attention should be given to government and private cooperation. Technical education should be given importance. Unfortunately the dependence of the national economy is on foreign loans. On the other hand the lavish spending of the government and bureaucracy are also unparalleled. Money is spent on unnecessary matters, or is spent in such places from which no development productive importance comes. In offices there is a culture of unnecessary use of resources. Important office-bearers have become habituated to corruption and there is no one to ask. Therefore, to stop the waste of wealth, there is a severe need for meaningful reforms in every sector of life. Hence the need is this, that non-development expenditures be controlled and serious efforts be made to stop corruption …",
