   "content": "<p>… adopted. Talks began between the two countries, and after detailed negotiation they reached an agreement. North Korea agreed to stop its atomic programme, in exchange for which America and Japan jointly gave North Korea two atomic reactors. A decade later this agreement fell into danger when the world began to say that North Korea has the capability to make atomic weapons.</p><p>Between the Palestinians and Israel, war has been going on for a long time over the establishment of a Palestinian state. In this war both parties have suffered severe financial and human losses. The Israeli army is attacking Palestinians, while Palestinian armed organisations are targeting Israel. Through the mediation of the American government, in 1993 negotiations began in Oslo (Norway) between Palestinian representatives and Israel. After long negotiations both parties agreed on a declaration of principles. In it the Palestinian leadership (Yasser Arafat) recognised Israel, and Israel showed willingness for the phased transfer of power in the Palestinian-majority areas. This negotiation was continued, and after the agreements of 1994-95, under the leadership of Mahmoud Abbas, the Palestinian National Authority was established. The Palestinians were given autonomy in the Gaza Strip and some parts of the West Bank of the River Jordan. After this, talks began between Jordan and Israel and an agreement took place between the two countries.</p><p>The disputes after the Pak-India war of 1965 were resolved through negotiation and the mediation of the Soviet Union by means of the Tashkent agreement. The disputes after the Pak-India war of 1971 were resolved through mutual talks of the leadership of the two countries in the Indian city of Simla.</p><p>Causes of International Disputes</p><p>There are several important causes of international conflicts, and the most important is the issue of freedom. Most world problems in the world are because of freedom movements. Freedom is the right of every human being and nation. But when obstacles …</p>",
