   "content": "<p>… was done. The members also presented their proposals and recommended such a system in which human rights are respected. Measures of help and redress for the victims of racial discrimination were also proposed.</p><p>Mediation</p><p>For the effective resolution of conflicts the practical strategy of arbitration or mediation can also be adopted. In this respect the United Nations holds great importance. The Arab–Israel issue has given birth to several sub-conflicts. Because of differences over the use of the water of the River Jordan between Israel and Syria, and of the area vacated by the army, border clashes took place between the two countries. In the same way differences of Syria, Egypt, Lebanon and Jordan with Israel further increased. To control these affairs the United Nations made attempts at mediation but could not be successful. In the year 1967 a six-day war took place between the Arabs and Israel, in which the Egyptian air force was destroyed on the very first day of the war. Israel occupied the Gaza Strip and the Sinai peninsula. Israel also occupied East Bait-ul-Muqaddas, the West Bank of the River Jordan and the Golan areas. In November 1967 the Security Council of the United Nations, through resolution number 242, asked Israel for a conditional withdrawal from the occupied areas. The condition was that the Arab countries also recognise Israel and live in peace with it. However the parties were not ready to accept these conditions.</p><p>In 1947-48 the United Nations issued orders of ceasefire to stop the war going on in Kashmir between India and Pakistan. The United Nations established between Azad and Occupied Kashmir a temporary line by the name of the Line of Control (LOC). For the supervision of this line a United Nations supervisory military group was brought into being, and along with it this too was recognised: that the Kashmiris have the right of self-determination to decide their political future. But the parties, especially India, remain stuck on their stubbornness, and instead of the issue being solved it is becoming more complicated. The United Nations is an important institution for resolving world problems and conflicts, but the need is that this institution be made empowered so that it can get its decisions accepted.</p><p>If world leaders come forward with truthfulness and honesty, then any problem can be ended.</p><p>World and regional institutions too, if they want with honesty, can end any conflict, e.g. the Islamic …</p>",
