     "text": "In world problems and conflicts, individuals of world fame can play a prominent role as mediators and for negotiation. In the past such personalities have also played a role. The Secretary General of the United Nations, because of the importance of his office, is an acceptable personality at the world level. No country can easily ignore his word or opinion. According to the charter of the United Nations he is also a diplomat and mediator. He has the ability to create world consensus of opinion on world problems. The Secretary General of the United Nations, Ban Ki-moon, had gone to Ankara to take part in a world conference held on the issue of Somalia, where, taking the opportunity, he requested the government of Turkey that Turkey resolve its problems with Cyprus and Armenia in a peaceful manner. Addressing the Turkish leadership at a university in Istanbul, he said: “Come! Establish new diplomatic relations with Armenia. Come! Benefit from the opportunities in Cyprus. You smooth the path.” Hence the Secretary General of the United Nations, setting aside traditional powers and role, can help in resolving problems in political ways.",
