   "content": "<p>2. Arbitrating or getting negotiation done is an art; therefore the mediator should have the ability to understand the psychology of the parties. The mediator’s attention should be on this, from what angles the parties like to see things in the future. The mediator should go forward keeping his hand on the pulse of the parties.</p><p>3. A good mediator should be experienced. The more experience, the more quickly and easily the matter will be solved. Therefore the mediator should be experienced, cool-tempered and patient. If he is emotional and hot-tempered, then instead of the issue being solved it can become worse.</p><p>4. The environment has a great effect on negotiations, talks and arbitration. The mediator or negotiator should have the ability to keep an eye on the environment. The mediator should keep the environment under his control but should not try to influence the participants and the decision.</p><p>5. It is necessary for the mediator that he ensures a moderate, calm, safe and pleasant environment.</p><p>6. It is also necessary for the mediator to be a person of character. The mediator should play such a role that both parties are satisfied with his character.</p><p>7. It is necessary for the negotiator that he is expert in those matters on which there is difference, so that the root of the issue can be reached easily. It is also extremely important for the mediator to be just.</p><p>8. The mediator should be just and educated.</p><p>How to Adopt Qualities of A Good Mediator and Negotiator</p><p>Every human being can adopt the qualities of a good mediator and negotiator. The first thing is that in every human being there should be the spirit of resolving problems and conflicts. The aim of human life is that peace be established in human society. If closeness to those who arbitrate and negotiate is obtained and their activities are watched, then this art can be learned. For this purpose observation and study is also very necessary, through which knowledge of the requisites of arbitration and negotiation can be obtained …</p>",
