   "theory": "… can be obtained. One should take part in the arbitration and negotiation activities taking place in one’s own home, family and village or city, and keep every aspect in view. To become a mediator there should be a spirit of sacrifice. One should be a selfless servant. The best mediator or negotiator can be the one who has in him the courage to give human and financial sacrifice, because in this path a person has to pay the price of personal loss too. Justice should be made a necessary part of life, because the aim of arbitration and negotiation is the just decision of the conflict. To become a mediator, besides law and customs, acquaintance with religious commands and teachings is also necessary, because most decisions have to be made in the light of law, customs and religious principles. Good decisions are those that become the durable solution of conflicts. The qualities of a mediator or negotiator have been stated above. If most of these qualities are adopted, then anyone can become a mediator and negotiator. It is necessary for a good citizen that he has the ability of arbitration of conflicts and talks between parties.",
