   "content": "<p>2. For the following questions, choose the suitable answer, i.e. (a), (b), (c) or (d), and write it in the box given against each question:</p><p>1. In 1917 the Palestinian region went from ________ into the control of Britain.</p><p>(a) Iran  (b) Afghanistan  (c) China  (d) Turkey</p><p>2. On eleventh September 2001 air attacks took place on the World Trade Center New York and the Pentagon of ________ .</p><p>(a) Canada  (b) Britain  (c) Japan  (d) America</p><p>3. In October 2006 North Korea carried out an underground ________ explosion.</p><p>(a) gunpowder  (b) destructive  (c) atomic  (d) recreational</p><p>4. Among the causes of both world wars, the race of ________ between countries is also included.</p><p>(a) power  (b) greed  (c) money  (d) weapons</p><p>5. Through Kosygin’s efforts a peace agreement was made between Pakistan and India in ________ .</p><p>(a) Tashkent  (b) Samarkand  (c) Bukhara  (d) Delhi</p><p>6. For a mediator, being ________ -loving is also extremely important.</p><p>(a) justice  (b) tradition  (c) reaction  (d) revolution</p><p>3. Mark the correct sentences as “correct” and the wrong sentences as “wrong” in the following:</p><p>1. On eleventh September 2011 air attacks took place on America’s World Trade Center and the Pentagon. (correct / wrong)</p><p>2. America attacked Iraq in March 2003. (correct / wrong)</p><p>3. After the Pak-India war of 1965 the Tashkent agreement was made. (correct / wrong)</p><p>4. For the resolution of conflicts mediation is an ineffective way. (correct / wrong)</p><p>5. At this time the most dangerous region of the world is the land of Jordan. (correct / wrong)</p><p>6. The Line of Control is a temporary border between Pakistan and China. (correct / wrong)</p><p>7. The aim of negotiation is to make a just decision of conflicts. (correct / wrong)</p><p>8. North Korea has atomic weapons. (correct / wrong)</p><p>4. Match the columns:</p><p>5. Give short answers to the following questions:</p><p>1. When and where did the Israeli state come into being?</p><p>2. What is the Line of Control?</p><p>3. When and where was the Oslo agreement made, and what were its important points?</p><p>4. State the characteristics of a mediator or negotiator.</p><p>6. Give detailed answers to the following questions:</p><p>1. Write the historical background of present world conflicts.</p><p>2. Identify the causes of world conflicts.</p><p>3. What can be the effective strategies for the resolution of conflicts?</p><p>4. Write a note on the role of the United Nations in world arbitration and the functions of the International Court of Justice.</p><p>5. State the role of individuals for arbitration and negotiation in international conflicts.</p>",
