     "text": "There are different sources of collecting information, for example observation, interviews, questionnaires, the study of documents and the use of the internet. Information is collected on a particular topic. Written information is collected in a file. Audio and video information is collected in electronic equipment, and information obtained from the internet is saved in the computer. Whether little or much information is obtained about the topic, it is in any case necessary to keep it safe. Now the collected information is arranged in the light of several criteria. That is, written material is kept on one side, recorded information on the other side, and computer information collected on another side. Then this information is arranged on the basis of reliable sources, reliable writers, time and place, and nearness to the topic. They are given page numbers, and if necessary notes are written with a pencil. Unnecessary material is separated with respect to the topic. Now the study of the collected and arranged material is started. A good thing is that one’s study is also written down. Along with this it is also necessary that references too be written. One important thing is that collected material, whether necessary or unnecessary, should not be wasted after study and review. Arranging the material, closing it in a file, the note and date about the material should be written on top. It is possible that this very material is useful in some research or investigation. This collected and arranged material is the result of long labour and also a reliable reference; therefore its protection is necessary.",
