   "content": "<p>1. Identification of the problem:</p><p>First of all the problem is identified, that is, what the problem is and what the importance of this problem is. The establishment of a stable society is the responsibility of all of us. Before the problem raises its head and becomes complicated, there is a need to understand it and identify it. For example, weaknesses in the examination system are an important problem.</p><p>2. Three or four possible solutions of the problem:</p><p>Now at least three or four possible solution hypotheses of this problem will have to be presented. For example, for reform in the examination system the following possible solution hypotheses are:</p><p>(a) Every month the teacher prepares a review report of his pupils, and numbers be fixed for these reports.</p><p>(b) Corrupt employees be removed from the examining institutions and employees of good reputation be encouraged. Professional people be discouraged and kept away from examination duties. Honest people be appointed examiners and encouraged.</p><p>(c) The system of checking at examination centres be made effective. The process of preparing papers and checking be made effective, and honest teachers be employed to end the possibilities of injustice in it.</p><p>(d) The incentives of examination staff be increased satisfactorily.</p><p>3. Advantages and disadvantages of every possible solution:</p><p>To find the best solution a detailed critical review of every possible solution has to be taken. For example, every month the teacher prepares a review report of his pupils and numbers are fixed for these reports. Its benefit will be that the real ability of the child can be estimated. At the very basic level a correct review can also be taken. The teacher’s dignity too will not be hurt. Students too will be saved from troubles. Its disadvantage is that the teacher can work by personal liking and disliking, but even so its possibilities are less. The second solution is that corrupt staff be discouraged and honest people be encouraged. This too is a good thing …</p>",
