   "content": "<p>By adopting this kind of policy good people will come into the field, because they will be encouraged. But this is a difficult act, and testing every teacher is not so easy. Another proposal is to make the system of checking and inspection effective. Its benefit is that errors will be fewer and no one’s rights will be violated. Its disadvantage is that in the early stages of the examination this solution may perhaps not prove so effective. The last solution is that the incentives of the examination staff be increased satisfactorily. Its good point is that the staff will be financially satisfied and improvement will come in the examination system. Its weakness is that if, despite incentives, they do not desist, then this system will again remain a victim of failure and corruption.</p><p>4. Recommendation of the best solution:</p><p>After taking a thorough critical review of all the proposals, it can be decided what the best solution to the problem is. Reviewing the said proposals, it can be said that proposal number one is more useful.</p><p>Methods to Disseminate Information</p><p>Different methods are used for the dissemination of information and news, of which the important ones are the following:</p><p>Newsletters</p><p>By newsletter is meant that published information or news which relates to the interests of some particular group. This kind of information is spread among the members and employees of society or institutions at fixed times. In accordance with this method, continuous information is provided to the members of interest groups and organisations about the activities of their organisation and its interests etc. Most institutions provide the general public with information about that institution and its activities, published after a particular period.</p><p>Bulletin Boards</p><p>A bulletin is called a thematic news item. Any official announcement too is called a bulletin. Bulletin boards can be taken in two senses. A simple and common meaning is that any notice or information is pinned on the notice board of an institution …</p>",
