   "content": "<p>Exercise</p><p>1. Fill in the blanks in the following sentences with suitable words:</p><p>1. Information obtained from the internet is ________ .</p><p>2. They are collected by obtaining them from different reliable ________ sources.</p><p>3. There are several ________ search in computer internet.</p><p>4. Today knowledge is incomplete without the use of computer and ________ .</p><p>5. Collected and arranged material is the result of a long ________ .</p><p>2. For the following questions, choose the suitable answer, i.e. (a), (b), (c) or (d), and write it in the box given against each question:</p><p>1. The internet has ________ every part of the world together.</p><p>(a) separated  (b) tied  (c) highlighted  (d) made to fight</p><p>2. On ________ all kinds of information and websites are present.</p><p>(a) CD  (b) cassette  (c) internet  (d) ship</p><p>3. In multinational countries the ________ form of government fails.</p><p>(a) parliamentary  (b) federal  (c) democratic  (d) unitary</p><p>4. Collected and ________ material is the result of long labour.</p><p>(a) arranged  (b) wasted  (c) studied  (d) heated</p><p>5. Any ________ announcement too is called a bulletin.</p><p>(a) old  (b) known  (c) official  (d) humorous</p><p>3. Mark the correct sentences as “correct” and the wrong sentences as “wrong” in the following:</p><p>1. The meaning of internet is “fishing net”. (correct / wrong)</p><p>2. No government documents are present on the internet. (correct / wrong)</p>",
