   "content": "<p>Exercise</p><p>1. Fill in the blanks in the following sentences with suitable words:</p><p>1. Political parties are the spokesmen of public wishes and ________ .</p><p>2. The vote should always be given by looking at a party’s ________ or programme.</p><p>3. Modern social movements are now using modern technology and ________ .</p><p>4. An independent judiciary alone plays an important role in the establishment of a ________ and welfare system.</p><p>5. People talk of rights but turn away from their ________ .</p><p>2. For the following questions, choose the suitable answer, i.e. (a), (b), (c) or (d), and write it in the box given against each question:</p><p>1. In July 1972 a peace agreement was made between India and Pakistan at ________ .</p><p>(a) Shimla  (b) Bombay  (c) Agra  (d) Delhi</p><p>2. For the extension of Karachi Steel Mills ________ provided one billion dollars.</p><p>(a) China  (b) Iran  (c) Mongolia  (d) Russia</p><p>3. The Muslim League government for the first time gave the State Bank of Pakistan ________ .</p><p>(a) leave  (b) money  (c) autonomy  (d) punishment</p><p>4. The media played a role to the point of perfection in the ________ of people in every field.</p><p>(a) awakening  (b) hurting  (c) misery  (d) difficulties</p><p>5. In society people will have to be taught tolerance, ________ and forbearance.</p><p>(a) awakening  (b) labour  (c) acceptance  (d) courage</p><p>3. Mark the correct sentences as “correct” and the wrong sentences as “wrong”:</p><p>1. There is no special difference between the constitutions of political parties and the national constitution. (correct / wrong)</p><p>2. It is not necessary to see whether political parties acted upon most promises or not. (correct / wrong)</p><p>3. For a stable political system the opposition is no less than deadly poison. (correct / wrong)</p><p>4. Political parties and social movements are two names of one thing. (correct / wrong)</p><p>5. Industrial development gave birth to many organisations and movements. (correct / wrong)</p><p>6. Pakistan, because of present world problems, is a victim of extremism. (correct / wrong)</p><p>7. Problems are always solved with the gun. (correct / wrong)</p>",
