   "content": "<p>Peace</p><p>Peace is called the opposite of war, and its different definitions are somewhat as follows:</p><p>1. According to the Encarta Encyclopedia, “Peace is the name of freedom from war or conflict, a condition free from noise and chaos, and non-violence and absence of chaos in the country.”</p><p>2. According to the Advanced Oxford Dictionary, “Peace is called the condition free from anxiety, noise and chaos.”</p><p>3. According to Chambers Advanced Practical Dictionary, “Peace is the name of the condition of reconciliation, calm, safety and contentment.”</p><p>War and violence are inhuman acts, and causing harm to anyone’s life and property through them is an immoral activity. In history the concept of peace has always been connected with ethics, divine will and economic and social utility. No moral code or religion wants unrest. The majority of people desire peace.</p><p>A big cause of unrest in the countries of the Third World is that some individuals or groups use force illegally, although according to the constitution and law the authority to use force belongs only to government institutions. However the government too should not use force without need. Governmental power should be used only in such circumstances when national or collective interests demand it.</p><p>Importance of Peaceful Society</p><p>The basic purpose of human society, state and government and law is the establishment of peace. Before the establishment of social life and institutions there was unrest. There was no calm in man’s life. Difficulties and lawlessness had made life miserable. If studied carefully, social life came into being to face human difficulties, dangers and troubles, which first of all …</p>",
