     "text": "At the world level the effects of wars are of importance. After wars feelings of revenge arise, which become the cause of some dangerous clash. Insecurity and revenge compel nations to the arms race. Its bright example is the nuclear arms race in North Korea, Iran, Pakistan, India and China etc. Wars between nations as a result become the cause of world terrorism and extremism. After wars economic crises arise. Not only the defeated countries but the winners too face economic crisis. After World War Two Britain was among the winners, but it was so war-stricken that Britain gave independence to many colonies. The events after wars also become the cause of political upheaval …",
