   "content": "<p>6. Non-acceptance and intolerance in human relations will have to be discouraged. Creating an environment of world tolerance is the most important need of the time. The world needs to act upon the policy of live and let live.</p><p>7. The world community too will have to say goodbye to the use of force and power in mutual relations. The path of dialogue and civility will have to be adopted.</p><p>To achieve these objectives serious efforts are needed at the world level. Countries too will have to play an active role seriously, and people and groups too will have to show activity.</p><p>Ways of Promoting Value Diversity in Pakistan</p><p>In Pakistan many ethnic groups live, and we have to live with this ethnic and linguistic diversity. This diversity is also a cause of positive competition and sustainable development. Value diversity can be strengthened through curriculum and education. For bringing positive change in any society curriculum and the system of education have great importance. The end of ignorance is the need of the time. Such material should be included in the course as creates tolerance, acceptance and forbearance in students. Priority should be given to education, and education should be not for employment but for humanity. It is necessary to include material creating ethnic and social harmony in the curriculum. Religion too can become a cause of the acceptance of value diversity. This can be made possible in Pakistani society, i.e. through the lesson of tolerance and forbearance; in fact the wrong interpretation of religion too can close the ways for value diversity. The clear message of Islam is human equality. Implementing Islamic teaching with its real spirit is the real solution of the matter, in which there is tolerance, there is cooperation, there is equality, which are the other faces of value diversity. Ulema and mashaikh can play a key role in creating harmony. This same harmony is value diversity. For this purpose the use of the pulpit and loudspeaker can prove very effective.</p><p>The media can be used for the lesson of human equality. Rather than unnecessary broadcasts it is better that …</p>",
