   "content": "<p>… provide training. For example, in an oil refining plant artificial fire is set somewhere and people are made to practise extinguishing the fire. However the mock action is carried out in a controlled environment where everyone is safe, while in a real event there are dangers to life.</p><p>Activities</p><p>1. Watch the proceedings of the session of international institutions on television or the internet.</p><p>2. Hold a session on the pattern of the General Assembly / Security Council of the United Nations.</p><p>For the said activities it is necessary to know about the structure and sessions of the General Assembly and the Security Council of the United Nations.</p><p>In the General Assembly of the United Nations all member countries have representation, and every country has the right of one vote. Every year a regular session of the Assembly is held. This session begins in the month of September on the day of the third Tuesday and generally concludes by Christmas. If the Security Council or a majority of its members files a request, special sessions of the Assembly can also be summoned. Every year a President and seventeen Vice-Presidents of the General Assembly are elected. The General Assembly is authorised to debate any subject. It can present recommendations to the Security Council and the member states. Without the permission of the Council the General Assembly is not authorised to debate those matters which are under consideration in the Security Council. Accepting its recommendations is not legally necessary. The General Assembly, except for some matters, can present resolutions with a simple majority. On important matters a two-thirds majority is needed, for example the issue of world peace and order, membership of the United Nations and financial affairs etc. are important matters.</p><p>The Security Council is in fact the executive of the United Nations. It has fifteen members, of which five countries, i.e. China, America, Russia, Britain and France, are permanent members, while ten are elected by the General Assembly for two years. Every month it elects its president. After every two weeks its session is held. Ordinary matters are decided …</p>",
