   "content": "<p>… favour, even then the matter will not be carried.</p><p>5. Finally, announce the decision of the Security Council.</p><p>Public Service Message</p><p>A public service announcement is a kind of advertisement which is presented through TV, radio or print media etc. The purpose of a standard public service message is to identify those problems in which awareness can be given to the public. Through it change can be brought in public attitudes. Historically, the public service announcement or public service message in its present form was started by the War Advertising Council during the Second World War. Through these advertisements the American public was to be taken into confidence about the different fronts of the war. After the war this council widened its plan of action further, and forest fires, blood donations and the safety of highways etc. were included in it. After a few years public service messages became more common on TV and radio. Today the preparation of this kind of message has been given the status of an industry, and it is also an important means of earning for the media.</p><p>Among the important topics of public service messages health and safety have importance. These messages are an essential part of awareness campaigns, and with time their topics keep increasing steadily. An example of this kind of message is also: “To protect your beloved earth, keep it green.” The support of public service messages can be taken about religious, cultural, social, political, legal, moral and military etc. matters. In preparing this message many things have to be kept in view, for example the choice of effective words, the selection of the best voices and faces and the selection of an effective background etc.</p><p>What do you want to tell the world? This is the important question, taking which as the basis you present the public service message. This question too is important: which words will you use which, besides being fit to be presented on radio and television, also fulfil your purpose? The things which have to be thought about and understood are: what, when, where and how. The most important thing is to see that the words and sentences of your message are clear and not ambiguous for listeners or viewers. Taking care of brevity is of great importance …</p>",
