   "content": "<p>Signature Campaign</p><p>A signature campaign is such a plan in which the signatures of the greatest number of people are obtained in favour of or against some issue, so that they gain awareness about the issue and pressure also increases on the concerned institutions. In Iran a powerful signature campaign was run for the rights of women. The campaign of one million signatures was run by Iranian women for the rights of women. In a political demonstration the participants can be beaten, suppressed or arrested, but in a signature campaign two or three workers go to cities and obtain signatures at shops, parks, recreational places, bus stops, schools and other public places. Suppressing this campaign is very difficult, because it is a peaceful and effective means of conveying one’s point to authorised people. In a signature campaign people are explained to face to face and then, according to their will, their signature is taken. In this way the message spreads to every corner of the country. Its most important purpose is to create awareness and feeling among people.</p><p>A signature campaign of this same kind was run by the All Parties Hurriyat Conference, the representative party alliance of Kashmir. Its purpose was to draw the attention of American President Barack Hussain Obama to the Kashmir dispute. A spokesman of the All Parties Hurriyat Conference said in a statement that this campaign was run in Jammu and Azad Kashmir for two weeks. This document consisting of signatures was presented as a memorandum at the American Embassy in New Delhi.</p><p>Community Service</p><p>Community service means public service or activity based on donations. It is generally the activity of volunteers. But being a volunteer is also not necessary, because some people who join community service either take remuneration or have been bound to do so. For example, by some governments the compulsory responsibility of community service is placed on citizens. Military employees too are engaged in these activities. In schools and colleges, as training, community …</p>",
