   "content": "<p>(Ṭo’e)</p><p>Tab‘i halat (Physical Conditions): Physical, geographical conditions, outward situation; conditions related to land, water, natural resources and boundaries.</p><p>Tibbi (Physical): Concerned with health.</p><p>Tabaqati nizam (Class System): The presence of rich and poor and other discriminatory groups in a country.</p><p>(Ain)</p><p>‘Ilm (Science): Those facts which are obtained from observations and experiments.</p><p>‘Aqli (Rational): Whose basis is not on emotions but on thought and reflection.</p><p>‘Adam (Non existence, default): Not being.</p><p>‘Adam-e-maujudgi (Absence): Not being present.</p><p>‘Adam-e-istihkam (Instability): Not being stable; in which there is no stability.</p><p>‘Alami (Global): At the world level; in the whole world.</p><p>‘Adam-e-i‘timad (No-Confidence): Not having confidence.</p><p>Kasir-ul-aqwami corporations (Multi National Corporations): Such business institutions as work in several countries, e.g. Pepsi.</p><p>(Fe)</p><p>Fann (Art): Practical demonstration.</p><p>Fard (Individuals): Man or woman, whose plural is afrad.</p><p>Faraghat (Leisure): Free moments, moments of leisure.</p><p>Funun-e-latifa (Fine Arts): Those arts or human activities from which individuals may obtain pleasure.</p><p>Firqa-wariyat (Sectarianism): People of a religion being divided into groups on the basis of different styles of thought.</p><p>Fitri (Natural): Natural, i.e. according to the law of nature; those principles and regulations which are not artificial but exist in the universe.</p><p>Fariq riyasaten (State Parties): Those states which are parties to some dispute or treaty etc.</p><p>(Qaf)</p><p>Qanun-shikan (Offender): Those who break the law.</p><p>(Kaf)</p><p>Congress (Congress): An important political party of India; the name of the American law-making institution.</p><p>Kabina (Cabinet): Council of ministers. In Britain the king used to consult a small cabinet of eminent citizens of the country …</p>",
